  "body": "## Routine owner-correction record\nCraig rejected the scratch primitive R4 appearance and asked why existing Tripo mini-trucks and the established 3D workflow were not reused. This new docs-only branch records the stop and reuse requirement. It does not retry or publish the stopped R4 packet or touch PR355/506 branches.\n\n## Exact scope\nOnly project-management/boards/tokyo-drift-3d.md: td-197/198 status wording/date and the existing Garage stops paragraph. All other rows/owners and full acceptance gates are unchanged. Both tasks remain blocked; the old td-198 worker stays paused. No production admission, asset choice or authored mesh.\n\nRecover the intended original GLB/reference/manifest provenance, then independently inspect matched actual rendered evidence using the visual workflow and established anime pipeline before proposing adaptation. Do not silently relabel the existing Forge truck as the intended Tripo mini-truck. Unresolved identity is a narrow clarification after authorized read-only recovery, not a new permission gate for routine docs or audit.\n\n## Checks\nBase main 1b7ce64722405a91d633aa542da563b08a1c077a. Complete recursive tree returned truncated=false and contains no .github workflows or deployment configuration; ordinary docs-branch publication does not use an Actions workflow or deploy route. Diff bounded to three lines in one board file. Exact remote byte/head verification follows.\n\nNo merge, implementation, asset upload, game/site deployment, Actions dispatch or external-agent contact. Leave draft pending independent review.",
